  "golden_gate_reason": "Upstream is a pure source repo -- it ships no prebuilt .gb at any of these paths for build.py's own golden gate (hash-shipped-then-delete-then-rebuild-then-compare) to gate against. Verified instead against the c-sp/gameboy-test-roms v7.0 release bundle already vendored locally at cores/gb/tests/roms/mooneye-test-suite/ (untracked, gitignored, downloaded before this item): 104/115 built ROMs are byte-identical to that bundle; 11 differ by 4-18 bytes each at the same overall file size (add_sp_e_timing, oam_dma_start, ppu/vblank_stat_intr-GS, misc/ppu/vblank_stat_intr-C, and the boot_regs-* family). Root cause is the WLA-DX build: c-sp's release pins vhelin/wla-dx@d8b51a99 (per its assemble.sh), Veloce's toolchain pins the commit Mooneye's own CI uses, @89a90a56 (per the plan, section 5) -- two different, both-current WLA-DX commits producing functionally-equivalent but not byte-identical code for a handful of files. See rom_manifest.json for the sha256 this build produced; PROVENANCE.md has the full per-file comparison.",
